{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions","id":1533141,"title":"Making player characters out of \u201cvillainous\u201d factions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-25T16:44:22-07:00","id":1533141,"title":"Making player characters out of \u201cvillainous\u201d factions","content":"So the other day I made my very first World of Darkness character. I was fascinated by the powers of the Tzimisce clan, so I went and made one in V20, not as a depraved flesh-warping artist of torment and oh god why is it still alive, but as a cheerfully unhinged back-alley doctor with a generally friendly disposition even as he digs bullets out of your brain and gives you extra eyes because your forehead looked a little too empty. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I took one of the \u201cdesignated antagonist\u201d clans and made a character who isn\u2019t just \u201cnot immediately repulsive\u201d but actually <i>fun</i>.<br /> <br /> So I was just wondering: how might you guys go about doing that for the Red Talons? Make somebody who actually works as a member of a group that isn\u2019t entirely composed of other Talons, and isn\u2019t a totally insufferable and violent misanthrope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T17:05:26-07:00","id":1533142,"title":"","content":"Red Talons are villainous?<br /> <br /> Nah, Red Talons are very relatable. They get shat on every single day and none of the other Garou give a fuck.....that fuck in the Dodge over their murdered three of your siblings last year but if you so much as look sideways at him half a dozen Homids crawl out of the woodwork to tell you not to overreact and to ' try to understand his point of view'.....fuck that noise.<br /> <br /> If the Lodge or the Dying Cubs are a bridge too far just play a Warder, you have your territory and the humans have theirs. You stay out of theirs and they stay out of yours.......if they don't well then they pay the price they shoot kids for knocking on their door you eat their face for pissing on your patch.....surely your being far more reasonable than they are? Hell, you even like some of your Homid packmates families, as long as they keep to their places,......family is everything to a Talon, its why the Curse and the damage that a First Change can do to their birth pack is so devastating......sure your Garou Pack becomes your new family but its not quite the same.<br /> <br /> Or be a Whelp and just know that some humans are pretty alright really and totally shouldn't be killed.......not those guys, those guys over there need to die......but your buds? Nah, they're cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T18:25:17-07:00","id":1533145,"title":"","content":"Read the Revised tribebook, it's great.<br /> <br /> Red Talons aren't really that hard to make work in a group, at least outside an urban setting. Just make one who's low rage and high willpower/gnosis and have their pragmatism outweigh their anger. People often play Red Talons as dumb or simple, but that's a mistake. They're clever; they successfully built up a black ops division, the Winter Packs, with only one Garou outside the tribe finding out. During the Middle Ages, their use of the Night-Fear displayed a pretty sophisticated understanding of psychological warfare, even if it didn't end up working out for them. So why would one work with other Garou and not Kill All Humans? Because it benefits the tribe, Griffon's brood, or Gaia to restrain themselves. Or maybe they just know they won't get their way and don't feel like trying to argue about it at every opportunity, even if it rankles.<br /> <br /> As far as making them sympathetic? That's simple. Emphasize that their hatred of humans is due to material concerns, namely that they're being wiped out. There is also psychological trauma; many Red Talons has had experiences at the hands of humans that would inflict PTSD simply because that's common for wolves. Then after their first change they hang around a bunch of other people who suffered the same traumas and the spirits of extinct and endangered animals. And you can sure bet that when they learn how humans wiped out most wolves, there's a little voice in the back of their head saying, &quot;Oh Gaia, we're next.&quot; Like Damian May says, humans are using their families as rugs. 30% of the wolf population dies a year from humans and it wasn't too long ago wolves were extirpated in much of Europe and North America. They still are in many places. You know how you felt towards the aliens in <i>Independence Day</i>, how you didn't think twice about killing them off and wanted the bastards dead? That's how the Red Talons feel about humans. They do not care about humanity's internal divisions because when you are on the receiving end of genocidal violence all that looks pretty irrelevant. Even the humans who say they're against killing wolves tend not to do much about it.<br /> <br /> There's room for other character concepts. You can have a Talon meet a shapeshifted mage and come to the conclusion that there are ways to make humans no longer human anymore. You can have one decide that no matter how un-wolf-like it feels, if divisions among the Garou can harm them, turnabout is fair play and they should aggravate divisions among the humans. You can have one decide that the real problem is that any species could do what humans have done--so while they have to utterly break humanity's power, the species itself doesn't have to die. You can have one who thinks extinction before a species' time is inherently abhorrent (a view Griffon shares, by the way) and so hates the thought of entirely wiping out the human species. I've explored those concepts in my own play. But I wouldn't drop the misanthropy. As far as the Talons are concerned, they are at war with humanity. They may have different ideas on how to fight that war or how to win it than the rest of the tribe, but they're still at war.<br /> <br /> The Whelps often get brought up in these conversations, but they've always rubbed me the wrong way--the more in-depth look we get at them in Revised makes them seem naive by placing a large chunk of the responsibility for humanity's actions on an external force (the Wyrm/vampires). That's the sort of thing which will make most humans and homid Garou feel good, but it's wrong. There's no Wyrm or vampires in real life and we did the same shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T19:18:44-07:00","id":1533147,"title":"","content":"A lot of people will get defensive on that last point and claim that Garou could have turned the opinions of humanity around if the Impergium hadn't happened, but the numbers would have always been against Garou on that kind of front, and that was the job of the Apis, so really, it was the War of Rage that hurt them the most on that front.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't get why the Red Talons' beef is that difficult a thing for readers to understand, but I've been an off one for a while. Maybe it was reading (and later watching) Watership Down when I was in the 5th grade...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T19:32:28-07:00","id":1533148,"title":"","content":"The cynical answer:<br /> <br /> If you got the Red Talon's beef it would mean thinking you're complicit in doing bad stuff. Most people don't like thinking they're complicit in doing bad stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T00:02:45-07:00","id":1533156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533148#post1533148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cynical answer:<br /> <br /> If you got the Red Talon's beef it would mean thinking you're complicit in doing bad stuff. Most people don't like thinking they're complicit in doing bad stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than that, a lot of people don't like that the Red Talons don't see humans as the most specialest species. They see humans as a very real threat and they aren't wrong. They aren't misanthropes, they just don't think a human life is worth as much as a wolf's.<br /> <br /> One of my favourite ways to explore Red Talons, is to explore how they pretty much force themselves to ignore any higher reasoning. But in doing so they are effectively creating an internal stereotype of what a true wolf IS. When wolves are fairly varied in how they live, be it scavengers, fishers, huge mafia-style packs (hi Yellowstone) or family units.<br /> <br /> Or that Red Talons are the only tribe other than Bone Gnawers who are willing to go to places other garou refuse to go. There are Red Talons in Africa who are Cape Hunting Dogs, there are Red Talons in Australia who are Dingo. Yet others of the tribe haaate this, because those garou aren't True Wolves.<br /> <br /> Red Talons also have culture and writing, they aren't just living as wolves. One of my favourite PCs was a Crinos-born (though in Chernobyl so he was a radiation created one) Galliard Red Talon who TRIED to get others to see his tribe as something other than balls of anger.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue with Red Talons in games comes from people who play a ball of Rage that refuses to budge. Which is a bad character regardless of their B/A/T.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T06:15:25-07:00","id":1533164,"title":"","content":"It's also kind of ironic that they try to force themselves to ignore higher reasoning given that spirits had it prior to humans ever evolving. Griffon has it, you want to tell <i>him</i> he's got a human-mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T07:50:08-07:00","id":1533169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533164#post1533164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also kind of ironic that they try to force themselves to ignore higher reasoning given that spirits had it prior to humans ever evolving. Griffon has it, you want to tell <i>him</i> he's got a human-mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's what shows they are still garou; They have decided what a wolf should be and stick to it, even if it is not good long term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T13:00:12-07:00","id":1533195,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons are one of my favorite tribes, and imo one of the most misunderstood and tragic. I feel when others try to cast them as villains, that they merely haven't read much about them as a tribe, much like I feel others see Kalaril (younger brother) as a villainous tribe. I firmly believe WtA wouldn't even be WtA without them. Their most powerful gifts are all oriented towards healing Gaia in many ways (and not just feeding the land) and towards reading prophecy. The prophecy of apocalypse originated from this tribe, even. I feel like people's brains shut down when they hear about a tribe that hunts humans, ignoring that there are rites across most of the tribes that touch on this exact theme, from bone gnawer to coggie.<br /> <br /> Desperation is the primary motivator of this tribe's actions. Seeing generation after generation of their families wiped out by humans both directly and indirectly, not hatred. They're no more villainous than an injured bear or a cornered mountain lion. They are alien in their thinking and mannerisms to be certain, because they aren't human. That's the start and end of it. Many of my favorite characters I've played are Red Talons.<br /> <br /> There are many ways to go about it, but having one driven by prophecy to cooperate would be completely canon. One that learned through war how to collaborate with humans would work too (like the war of Chicago, hunting vampires.) Perhaps one is following the directive of a personal patron to bring a prophecy to others, or perhaps is cooperating with a pack of homids with the specific purpose of teaching them how to be wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T13:57:19-07:00","id":1533198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533195#post1533195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Talons are one of my favorite tribes, and imo one of the most misunderstood and tragic. I feel when others try to cast them as villains, that they merely haven't read much about them as a tribe, much like I feel others see Kalaril (younger brother) as a villainous tribe. I firmly believe WtA wouldn't even be WtA without them. Their most powerful gifts are all oriented towards healing Gaia in many ways (and not just feeding the land) and towards reading prophecy. The prophecy of apocalypse originated from this tribe, even. I feel like people's brains shut down when they hear about a tribe that hunts humans, ignoring that there are rites across most of the tribes that touch on this exact theme, from bone gnawer to coggie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is also that they don't allow homids, so the tribe is seen as only for those who hate people. I guess because the ones doing it either don't like the idea of lupus (shock jockeying/edgy says TV Tropes) or don't like the critique on modern world.<br /> <br /> I have seen people say that hunting wolves is justified, because garou had the Impegrium. So it is just payback. And in general the idea of killing humans is treated as the worst thing to do, while killing wolves is just shrugged about.<br /> <br /> But I have to say that Red Talons get bad reputation not just due to the above. I have witnessed many Red Talons who join a game and at even the tiniest moment they have to compromise, they start acting like a 5-year old child throwing a tantrum ft.frenzy. I don't mean they push back, I mean they decide the much higher ranked homid needs to be defeated/killed. Some 'guides' to the tribe even used to say Red Talons are ALL about the Alpha/Omega stuff, ESPECIALLY picking the omega and dominating them. One memorable 'tribal lore' explanation even said that a fostern Talon has HEARD of the Litany.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the tantrum throwing Talons aren't as common now. But that is also because they are rarely allowed in games.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:31:35-07:00","id":1533201,"title":"","content":"To my understanding, they have a reputation of \u201cpsychotic misanthropes who genuinely believe that every individual human is a servant of the Wyrm and needs to die NOW, along with anyone who thinks anything more or other than that.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:43:11-07:00","id":1533202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533201#post1533201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my understanding, they have a reputation of \u201cpsychotic misanthropes who genuinely believe that every individual human is a servant of the Wyrm and needs to die NOW, along with anyone who thinks anything more or other than that.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know there is not a single Talon who thinks this in the source material at all. Even the most extremist Predator King doesn't want to kill all Garou who don't agree with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:45:39-07:00","id":1533203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533198#post1533198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is also that they don't allow homids, so the tribe is seen as only for those who hate people. I guess because the ones doing it either don't like the idea of lupus (shock jockeying/edgy says TV Tropes) or don't like the critique on modern world.<br /> <br /> I have seen people say that hunting wolves is justified, because garou had the Impegrium. So it is just payback. And in general the idea of killing humans is treated as the worst thing to do, while killing wolves is just shrugged about.<br /> <br /> But I have to say that Red Talons get bad reputation not just due to the above. I have witnessed many Red Talons who join a game and at even the tiniest moment they have to compromise, they start acting like a 5-year old child throwing a tantrum ft.frenzy. I don't mean they push back, I mean they decide the much higher ranked homid needs to be defeated/killed. Some 'guides' to the tribe even used to say Red Talons are ALL about the Alpha/Omega stuff, ESPECIALLY picking the omega and dominating them. One memorable 'tribal lore' explanation even said that a fostern Talon has HEARD of the Litany.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the tantrum throwing Talons aren't as common now. But that is also because they are rarely allowed in games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interpreting the Red Talons as a stepping stone to crossing over with the Omegaverse is... a new one, to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my understanding, they have a reputation of \u201cpsychotic misanthropes who genuinely believe that every individual human is a servant of the Wyrm and needs to die NOW, along with anyone who thinks anything more or other than that.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The reputation of the Garou among non-Garou isn't much different than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:46:24-07:00","id":1533204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533201#post1533201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my understanding, they have a reputation of \u201cpsychotic misanthropes who genuinely believe that every individual human is a servant of the Wyrm and needs to die NOW, along with anyone who thinks anything more or other than that.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this; There is an alien species that is higher tech than you. It has taken vast amounts of space that once belonged to humans and made it impossible to live there. They have also taken over stores and made it so a human cannot buy anything from there legally. In hunger, your brother tries to steal from the store but gets caught and shot. Later you find his skin in the alien living room.<br /> <br /> These aliens also hunt humans for sport, from their spaceships. They at times go into houses and kill parents, leaving the kids to starve.<br /> <br /> And all the while, they are poisoning everything so it gets harder and harder for humans to survive while they thrive. The aliens have alsd`o made this pseudo-human that is eternally around 14 and keep it as a pet.<br /> <br /> How hard would it be for you to not see these aliens as evil? How much sympathy could you have for them?<br /> <br /> This is what Red Talons face with humanity. So it is not that they are psychotic misanthropes hellbent on killing every human, they just wouldn't shed a tear for us. The 'every human must die NOW' Red Talons are badly played and don't really address WHY Talons hate humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:48:09-07:00","id":1533205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533203#post1533203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interpreting the Red Talons as a stepping stone to crossing over with the Omegaverse is... a new one, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not THAT Alpha/Omega thing XD More like &quot;I am an alpha and therefore I get to bully anyone I see as lesser.&quot;<br /> <br /> Things would be WAY nicer with ABO, ngl.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:50:34-07:00","id":1533207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533205#post1533205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not THAT Alpha/Omega thing XD More like &quot;I am an alpha and therefore I get to bully anyone I see as lesser.&quot;<br /> <br /> Things would be WAY nicer with ABO, ngl.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's hard not to go there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:59:19-07:00","id":1533209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is also that they don't allow homids, so the tribe is seen as only for those who hate people. I guess because the ones doing it either don't like the idea of lupus (shock jockeying/edgy says TV Tropes) or don't like the critique on modern world.<br /> <br /> I have seen people say that hunting wolves is justified, because garou had the Impegrium. So it is just payback. And in general the idea of killing humans is treated as the worst thing to do, while killing wolves is just shrugged about.<br /> <br /> But I have to say that Red Talons get bad reputation not just due to the above. I have witnessed many Red Talons who join a game and at even the tiniest moment they have to compromise, they start acting like a 5-year old child throwing a tantrum ft.frenzy. I don't mean they push back, I mean they decide the much higher ranked homid needs to be defeated/killed. Some 'guides' to the tribe even used to say Red Talons are ALL about the Alpha/Omega stuff, ESPECIALLY picking the omega and dominating them. One memorable 'tribal lore' explanation even said that a fostern Talon has HEARD of the Litany.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the tantrum throwing Talons aren't as common now. But that is also because they are rarely allowed in games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's also important to note that the whole alpha/omega thing stems largely from a fundamental misunderstanding of how wolf society operates, and is an understanding that continues to evolve. If one were to consider a tribe of Garou divorced from humanity, it would be a tribe that forms its foundations in the ways wolves relate to one another. If taken literally, a red talon's social structure would be more that of a family unit than a hierarchy (a decidedly human construct.) There's a few other wonky bits that get a double take from me, like the notion of the talons conceding to a singular kingly figure in Europe. If someone regularly saw their own family members regularly slaughtered (and those deaths debased by fellow homids) the response is suddenly a lot more relatable than merely the 'rarg must genocide humanity now' snidely whiplash villains so many cast them as. When a license to kill their family only costs 15 bucks one can hardly blame them for keeping other humans at arms length.<br /> <br /> Even setting aside a more modern understanding of wolf society I see them much less as misanthropes that mindlessly attack humans as servants of the Wyrm, so much as an alien tribe that other humans cant relate to, who blame humanity for most strongly enabling the Wyrm than anything else in the tellurian (and they're not wrong about that.) It's a game of telephone that debases who they are as a tribe more strongly attributed to players' resistance to reading and relying on rumors and oversimplified summaries than actually reading the materials. As you say, a big contributor to that frustration is the way other homid Garou dismiss their losses as being less significant than their own. If they have a vendetta beyond the typical thresholds of ordinary society, then it's more an implication that they're more victims of Griffin, using them as patsys for his own agenda having duped them into belief that this is the natural course of action to save Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:35:43-07:00","id":1533221,"title":"","content":"It does feel like it\u2019d be hard to present a Red Talon as anything besides a colossal jerk, assuming they even <i>have</i> a concept of morality (they\u2019re not human, after all). Survival, both individual and as a species, is the name of the game and they probably can\u2019t be bothered with complications.<br /> <br /> probably easier to make heroic than the dancers tho","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T18:18:00-07:00","id":1533225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533221#post1533221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does feel like it\u2019d be hard to present a Red Talon as anything besides a colossal jerk, assuming they even <i>have</i> a concept of morality (they\u2019re not human, after all). Survival, both individual and as a species, is the name of the game and they probably can\u2019t be bothered with complications.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Talons had no concept of morality they wouldn't be so outraged over the fate of extinct and endangered species. They wouldn't be upset at the prospect of abandoning their packmates and they wouldn't care about the fate of wolves. And why does the fact that they're not human mean they wouldn't have a concept of morality?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533221#post1533221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">probably easier to make heroic than the dancers tho</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you get how bad the Dancers are. The Talons will kill you and there's a <i>very</i> small number who will kill you slowly over a few days as part of a rite. The Dancers will get their jollies degrading you and using you as a plaything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 03-26-2024, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T19:26:35-07:00","id":1533226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533221#post1533221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does feel like it\u2019d be hard to present a Red Talon as anything besides a colossal jerk, assuming they even <i>have</i> a concept of morality (they\u2019re not human, after all). Survival, both individual and as a species, is the name of the game and they probably can\u2019t be bothered with complications.<br /> <br /> probably easier to make heroic than the dancers tho</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, humans are only heroes to themselves. Everything else carried on for ages before them, and their passing will not cause the universe to mourn or stop the world from spinning. Other social animals will continue to care for each other, to shelter their own, and go hunting for them when they cannot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T23:28:24-07:00","id":1533234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533221#post1533221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does feel like it\u2019d be hard to present a Red Talon as anything besides a colossal jerk</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that? Why would they be colossal jerks to other garou?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T01:41:57-07:00","id":1533237,"title":"","content":"Probably see them as too human and not wolf enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T05:21:52-07:00","id":1533242,"title":"","content":"I think overemphasizing negative qualities and therefore playing a PC from that faction as &quot;villainous&quot; or a &quot;colossal jerk&quot; would lead to problems all around, not just with the Red Talons. By that logic playing a Shadow Lord would mean playing a power-hungry backstabbing schemer who is secretly working against the other PCs or a Silver Fang would mean playing an arrogant asshole who believes he automatically deserves respect and a leadership-position because of his Tribe. In WOD pretty much all the factions have negative traits to some extent. VtM and MtA would present similar issues if you were to apply that logic. If the negative traits of any given faction are the only thing you focus on, they all end up becoming a hindrance to a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T05:50:26-07:00","id":1533245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533237#post1533237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably see them as too human and not wolf enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they do, other garou are still part wolves and they all are members of the same Nation. And unless the pack is nothing but Glass Walkers, there are plenty of tribes Talons get along with fine.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger question is; Would having a human-hating character break the story you want to tell and then ask why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T12:06:05-07:00","id":1533324,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons were obviously meant to be a more antagonistic tribe among the Garou, but I do not think they were meant to be villainous overall. They were simply an element that could provide easy drama in the same way the Shadow Lords or even Get of Fenris could be used. Early WtA was much more open to internal conflict within the Garou Nation then later editions. Many players conflate the entire Red Talon tribe with the camp of the Lodge of the Predator Kings. But in the 1e Players Guide, even the Lodge was mainly concerned with making alliances with the animal breeds of the other Fera for the future fight with mankind. Not killing all humans all the time. The Warders were primarily concerned with driving mankind away from the remaining areas of untouched wilderness and not necessarily killing them. While the anti-extinction faction was said to be the &quot;main camp.&quot; <br /> <br /> Now that stance was often undermined by other sourcebooks. Ways of the Wolf explicitly said that the first goal of the Red Talons was the destruction of humans, though this was limited by the Talons' fear that stupid and premature attacks would cause their small numbers to be wiped out. It also referred to the anti-extinction faction as &quot;small&quot; but growing. So clearly the writers were not on the same page as to which camps were to be dominant. I think the tribebooks and later sourcebooks would make the Warders camp the largest and inbetween politically the two other camps. But all of them did try to present the tribe as being somewhat divided, discussing options as to the best way forward, and being cautious in their attacks against humans.<br /> <br /> I think it's simply the case that many players and STs enjoy very extreme characters and presentations as an easy way to generate plot. So they ignore the presentation of a cautious tribe trying to balance their goals with their very limited resources, and openly debating what strategies work best and what opportunities can be seized.<br /> <br /> I think a bigger problem is the lack of any real description of Red Talon tribal culture and interests. Early tribes were presented almost exclusively through the dominant human culture of their homid breeds, so there was nothing to easily lift for a tribe that was all lupus. So without discussion of &quot;kill all humans&quot;, many players and STs simply did not know what to do with them. So they would keep falling back to that. I think what would have been nice is if in Caerns: Places of Power instead of placing the Red Talon caern just outside a human settlement, they would have had something be complete wilderness with almost no humans, and present a purely wilderness setting with some interesting spirits, monsters, and challenges that would provide conflict for the Red Talons absent from humans.<br /> <br /> So it definitely takes more work by STs to present the Red Talons in a way where they are not obvious villains and could add to - rather than detract from or blow up - the setting. But possibilities are there for those ambitious STs willing to work on it. But it's definitely one of the failings by the Developers to not properly address this and provide more tools for STs to incorporate them into chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T13:06:40-07:00","id":1533328,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as they are (at least in W20, no clue what\u2019s going on in W5) the Red Talons just seem conceptually difficult to make part of a player group without it being disruptive. The Talons just don\u2019t play nice with others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T14:03:00-07:00","id":1533330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533328#post1533328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as they are (at least in W20, no clue what\u2019s going on in W5) the Red Talons just seem conceptually difficult to make part of a player group without it being disruptive. The Talons just don\u2019t play nice with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this but virtually everyone in this thread has explained in detail why your assumptions are false and you can make them work in a PC group. The second chapter in their Revised tribebook opens with a Shadow Lord talking about how he was a member in a Red Talon-led pack and it worked out great until he (the Shadow Lord) fucked up and got most of the pack killed, for goodness sake.<br /> <br /> What you play or allow at your table is your prerogative. But this isn't impossible to make work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T16:26:29-07:00","id":1533335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533328#post1533328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as they are (at least in W20, no clue what\u2019s going on in W5) the Red Talons just seem conceptually difficult to make part of a player group without it being disruptive. The Talons just don\u2019t play nice with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 Red Talons make Legacy Red Talons look positively tsundere in comparison. You would never find the Red Talons of past editions engaging in biological warfare with hot contagious diseases, but one of the suggested character ideas in W5 is basically a Plague Dog who knows what they're doing and does it gladly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T17:07:21-07:00","id":1533338,"title":"","content":"Also it's stated that a good chunk, if not a majority, of W5 Talons are human-born, which eliminates a large chunk of their motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T17:25:48-07:00","id":1533341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533338#post1533338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it's stated that a good chunk, if not a majority, of W5 Talons are human-born, which eliminates a large chunk of their motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know it would actually hilarious if the majority of the Red talons who gone eco terrorist turned out to be actually humans and the wolf borne just want to chill in they territory .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T01:05:29-07:00","id":1533352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533328#post1533328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as they are (at least in W20, no clue what\u2019s going on in W5) the Red Talons just seem conceptually difficult to make part of a player group without it being disruptive. The Talons just don\u2019t play nice with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask yourself, why IS that? Why is a tribe dedicated to the protection of wilderness and wolves so alien compared to other garou? How much leeway are you giving the homids that you aren't the lupus?<br /> <br /> Because it isn't like other tribes don't have similar mentalities, just with their kinfolk spared. Talons are the mirror to Glass Walkers, but most tribes are between those extremes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-29-2024, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T01:33:11-07:00","id":1533353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533328#post1533328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as they are (at least in W20, no clue what\u2019s going on in W5) the Red Talons just seem conceptually difficult to make part of a player group without it being disruptive. The Talons just don\u2019t play nice with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>To echo what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> said: Ironically it's W5 that's 