ets mentioned are views in the Tribe like that the Wyrm is just a victim and the Weaver is the real threat which means that using the Wyrm's tools is completely fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again it would add a intresting wrinkle if it was made explicit that the human origin tribes members was responsible for that justification and the wolf born would rather stay in they frosts and slaughter the occasional tressspassers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T09:14:29-07:00","id":1533358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533354#post1533354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again it would add a intresting wrinkle if it was made explicit that the human origin tribes members was responsible for that justification and the wolf born would rather stay in they frosts and slaughter the occasional tressspassers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Griffin, producing a copy of W5: &quot;...And that's why I don't accept homid cubs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T12:15:12-07:00","id":1533363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533358#post1533358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Griffin, producing a copy of W5: &quot;...And that's why I don't accept homid cubs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it would funny if come shartted nation the red talons purged the human born members from the tribe and things go back to the status quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T13:23:40-07:00","id":1533900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533354#post1533354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again it would add a intresting wrinkle if it was made explicit that the human origin tribes members was responsible for that justification and the wolf born would rather stay in they frosts and slaughter the occasional tressspassers.</div> </div> </div> </div>so wait are you insinuating that the Red Talons that get all the press are like a Twitter mob, jumping into a cause they don\u2019t fully understand and making it everyone\u2019s problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T14:03:02-07:00","id":1533902,"title":"","content":"It's almost certainly the case that the Talons that would become the Dying Cubs live rent-free in the heads of the tribe's most fervent real-life detractors. Meanwhile, the majority of the tribe is like GLAD-OS in wolf form, in that they just want humanity gone (from their territory, and preferably from around most caerns, too), aka the Warders of the Land.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's your old friend, deadly volcanic gas. If I were you, I'd take a deep breath. And hold it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T17:39:15-07:00","id":1533916,"title":"","content":"I know that Voyd focused on the Red Talon, but taking advantage of the opportunity, how would it work to use some of the other &quot;villainous&quot; groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T17:57:47-07:00","id":1533919,"title":"","content":"I mean with BSDs it\u2019s impossible.<br /> <br /> Outside the Garou Nation, I made a Tzimisce who\u2019s a whimsical and macabre back-alley doctor.<br /> <br /> I feel like it\u2019d be relatively simple to make a friendly/heroic/noble Technocrat, but I am <i>terrified</i> of looking into Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T18:29:05-07:00","id":1533920,"title":"","content":"Firstly, don't say it's impossible, because there are a lot of people who like to play the villain, although with BSD it's too cumbersome, but it must be, secondly, there are other factions within the tribes themselves that have one behavior or another that someone here you might consider it amoral, in fact in the WOD in general there are a lot of amoral things if you look at it from a more boring perspective, but that's another story.<br /> <br /> For example: We have the Wiseguys mafia who in theory would not be good, as they are well... mafia so they are at best in the gray area.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords who take on the title of executioners and overthrow corrupt leaders and offenders of the litany, for the so-called greater good.<br /> <br /> Groups of Garou who work as mercenaries such as the Wayfares, Dies Ultima and possibly a Ronin, these services could yield dubious fame.<br /> <br /> Other Beasts like the Ratkins, Ananasi, Ajaba if you can call them &quot;villainous&quot; instead of villains.<br /> <br /> I'm just asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T19:12:58-07:00","id":1533923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533900#post1533900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so wait are you insinuating that the Red Talons that get all the press are like a Twitter mob, jumping into a cause they don\u2019t fully understand and making it everyone\u2019s problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean yeah that's basically it. Humanity is the only species on earth to to from some really bad takes due to our abilities of abstract reasoning and people have have gone to war over said bad takes. It could make for interesting scanero where wolf blooded red talons starts have problems with the human born since they antics is luring hunters to they cearns so some elements are planning on purging the human borns from the tribe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T19:22:29-07:00","id":1534007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533923#post1533923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean yeah that's basically it. Humanity is the only species on earth to to from some really bad takes due to our abilities of abstract reasoning and people have have gone to war over said bad takes. It could make for interesting scanero where wolf blooded red talons starts have problems with the human born since they antics is luring hunters to they cearns so some elements are planning on purging the human borns from the tribe...</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point, it's a matter of self-preservation. That would be the perfect time for a W5 Philodox to get up off their ass and lay down the law about not damaging the veil. Because not even the later Garou Nation was so shitty that it didn't know to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T19:30:33-07:00","id":1534008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1534007#post1534007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At that point, it's a matter of self-preservation. That would be the perfect time for a W5 Philodox to get up off their ass and lay down the law about not damaging the veil. Because not even the later Garou Nation was so shitty that it didn't know to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make for inserting dichotomy the red talons hate humans, but that's because as far they know humans are all crazed manacs that brings problems to territory...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T10:15:48-07:00","id":1534031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1533919#post1533919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean with BSDs it\u2019s impossible.<br /> <br /> Outside the Garou Nation, I made a Tzimisce who\u2019s a whimsical and macabre back-alley doctor.<br /> <br /> I feel like it\u2019d be relatively simple to make a friendly/heroic/noble Technocrat, but I am <i>terrified</i> of looking into Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, you were capable of doing it with a Tzimisce PC. That's in no way different to how you would handle that with the Red Talons and a PC belonging to that Tribe. There's so much of the WOD that operates in shades of grey. Even having darker factions like the Tzimisice or Red Talons doesn't go against the grain in the general WOD-atmosphere as far as PC-options are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T11:42:18-07:00","id":1534038,"title":"","content":"I think what people not familiar with WtA don't understand with the BSDs, is that they are not just a more cruel tribe. Unlike in vampire where there can be Tzimisce and Lasombra antribu, the BSDs are completely removed from the Nation. In fact, they are their OWN nation.<br /> <br /> Someone with BSD blood can join another tribe, but then they are members of THAT tribe and not BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T19:46:49-07:00","id":1535243,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons are definitely not a &quot;villainous&quot; tribe.<br /> <br /> But then, the Tzimisce aren't a villainous clan either, much less is the Technocratic Union a villainous faction. They're expected antagonists, that's a far different thing.<br /> <br /> Real equivalents to the BSDs are the Baali and the Nefandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T21:07:16-07:00","id":1535247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535243#post1535243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Talons are definitely not a &quot;villainous&quot; tribe.<br /> <br /> But then, the Tzimisce aren't a villainous clan either, much less is the Technocratic Union a villainous faction. They're expected antagonists, that's a far different thing.<br /> <br /> Real equivalents to the BSDs are the Baali and the Nefandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Tzims aren't villains, no one is. They call themselves Fiends, turn people into clothing and furniture on a lark, ham up performances as evil bastards, and they love every minute of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T21:27:41-07:00","id":1535249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535247#post1535247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Tzims aren't villains, no one is. They call themselves Fiends, turn people into clothing and furniture on a lark, ham up performances as evil bastards, and they love every minute of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Saying the Tzims are not villains is like saying that the Setites are just &quot;complex&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are not, or rather, they may even be complex, but they are also utterly and irredeemable villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T21:35:14-07:00","id":1535250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1534038#post1534038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what people not familiar with WtA don't understand with the BSDs, is that they are not just a more cruel tribe. Unlike in vampire where there can be Tzimisce and Lasombra antribu, the BSDs are completely removed from the Nation. In fact, they are their OWN nation.<br /> <br /> Someone with BSD blood can join another tribe, but then they are members of THAT tribe and not BSDs.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSD are the Baali from Vampire, the Nefandi from Mage and the Specters from WtO. Those are just basically irredeemable demons. They exist to destroy the world and nothing more. It's not possible to play those, unless the whole table is made up of these demons and you're playing some macabre game with the fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T02:13:00-07:00","id":1535255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535250#post1535250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BSD are the Baali from Vampire, the Nefandi from Mage and the Specters from WtO. Those are just basically irredeemable demons. They exist to destroy the world and nothing more. It's not possible to play those, unless the whole table is made up of these demons and you're playing some macabre game with the fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a lot of VtM players get tripped up by the Gaia vs Wyrm situation, assuming its Camarilla vs Sabbat but with werewolves. When its more like Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Inconnu vs Baali.<br /> <br /> Hence why you get people complaining about BSDs not being playable, they don't grasp the setting yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T07:43:09-07:00","id":1535263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535250#post1535250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BSD are the Baali from Vampire, the Nefandi from Mage and the Specters from WtO. Those are just basically irredeemable demons. They exist to destroy the world and nothing more. It's not possible to play those, unless the whole table is made up of these demons and you're playing some macabre game with the fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly impossible to play with any of them, maybe in bad taste depending on what you do, but it's still possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T08:47:44-07:00","id":1535272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535263#post1535263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not exactly impossible to play with any of them, maybe in bad taste depending on what you do, but it's still possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there actually is one exception among those I cited, which is the Specters. Because you actually CAN play a game with Specters, but with the caveat that it is done in a table about Specters ONLY. It's a &quot;Specters game&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the reason for that is because Specters are the only ones of the lot that aren't irredeemable, and the reason for that is because they actually still possess a &quot;good&quot; side inside of them, and it's a good side that wants to come out and it is an inalienable part of themselves. And I gotta say, I have storyteller-ed it once, and it's a great game, really really awesome (I 100% recommend people to try). But you won't just be playing some evil for evil's sake, it's actually a very deep and profound game with some heavy dark themes but beautiful lights of hope.<br /> <br /> However, for the Baali, BSDs and Nefandi, there's none of that. Behind each layer of evil there's just more of a douchebag bellow. Those are just irredeemable demons that just wanna watch the world burn. <br /> <br /> Sure you can play that if you wish, but it gets boring after a while. It is fun for a while to just not give a damn, but it gets boring.<br /> <br /> If you want to play an &quot;evil&quot; game, what I found out is that the fun way to do it without getting boring is to play a table that is AMORAL. To play some sort of being with a completely alien mindset.<br /> <br /> I achieved this playing Dark Ages Fae. Their alien mindset is awesome for that, and you can do the most unspeakable acts of &quot;evil&quot; without being actually &quot;evil&quot;. Wanna murder babies and torch an entire village? That's fine? Oh, for what reason you ask? What do you mean, we had a Pact with those humans, they failed to deliver their part, so that's the agreed upon consequence! That's just how things are, what are you talking about? Here is the contract, we explicitly said &quot;we will make you drink the blood of your children&quot;. I didn't hear you complain when we gave piles of gold to that other village before who also broke their oaths!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T09:06:30-07:00","id":1535273,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Dark Ages Fae, it was so funny the first time I ST it. One of my players was a &quot;Nazgul&quot; like winter fairy that had laid slumbering for a few hundreds years, only to wake up at the advent of Christianism (the game's premisse). So, he saw a couple of humans, wishing to now how things were going, and the tiny puny peasants lectured him about &quot;their lord and savior&quot;. I was just trying to get my player's character &quot;attuned to the times&quot;.<br /> <br /> To my surprise thou, my player didn't even blink, and before I even finished speaking about crucifixion and resurrection, my player just screamed &quot;I chop his head off!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And thus began my game, with the first village of peasants being beheaded, and a furious character leaving the place absolutely furious at the &quot;audacity of those humans&quot;, going towards the closest fairy enclave for answers. It was a heck of a fun game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T09:13:16-07:00","id":1535274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535255#post1535255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel a lot of VtM players get tripped up by the Gaia vs Wyrm situation, assuming its Camarilla vs Sabbat but with werewolves. When its more like Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Inconnu vs Baali.<br /> <br /> Hence why you get people complaining about BSDs not being playable, they don't grasp the setting yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I don't understand thou why some people can't understand this, unless if it is due to just the most superficial contact with WtA possible. I mean, the game makes it perfectly clear that the Wyrm is just some demonic force, and that the BSDs are forever gone madmen (mad-fera more precisely).<br /> <br /> Or that Vampire players, entrenched into a &quot;degrees of gray&quot; mindset, don't understand that WtA is set in a very black and white setting. Yes, werewolves can have varying degrees of gray morality, but the Wyrm has none of that. Likewise, there's some gray between Technocracy and Traditions, but there is NONE when the subject are the Nefandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T09:29:20-07:00","id":1535276,"title":"","content":"This is just me guessing, but I think you took it more to the side of ABSURD, than EVIL or AMORAL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T10:07:51-07:00","id":1535282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535274#post1535274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I don't understand thou why some people can't understand this, unless if it is due to just the most superficial contact with WtA possible. I mean, the game makes it perfectly clear that the Wyrm is just some demonic force, and that the BSDs are forever gone madmen (mad-fera more precisely).<br /> <br /> Or that Vampire players, entrenched into a &quot;degrees of gray&quot; mindset, don't understand that WtA is set in a very black and white setting. Yes, werewolves can have varying degrees of gray morality, but the Wyrm has none of that. Likewise, there's some gray between Technocracy and Traditions, but there is NONE when the subject are the Nefandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problems with having a shared universe, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T10:50:45-07:00","id":1535284,"title":"","content":"I think you can portray some Wyrm minions with gray morality. After all, vampires are of the Wyrm too, and people are fine representing them in various ways. Obviously on one far side of the spectrum, certain minions of the Wyrm just want to murder the world. But on the other side of the spectrum are just people making deals with the devil to get ahead in life to enjoy power, wealth, desire, etc. They may still do evil acts, but it's much more petty evil or limited in scale. Not every single fomori or monster are so depraved to be utterly unredeemable or have no good side. That doesn't mean they ultimately aren't enemies to the Garou or Gaia, but the Garou can prioritize which Wyrm minions need to be taken down first, or have the usual suspects among the Garou decide it's better to make deals with certain Wyrm minions so they can concentrate on greater threats.<br /> <br /> As ST I do try to have a full spectrum of different types of Wyrm minions (or people beginning to involve themselves with the Wyrm who don't understand what they're doing) so the game isn't completely about combat. Some Wyrm factions are obviously monstrous and need to be wiped out, but others might best be dealt with more subtle means or even negotiation. Some might even be best to ignore because there's so many other things to deal with. <br /> <br /> And since Wyrm taint is so nebulous, not everyone who has Wyrm taint is actually any kind of enemy. They're just been involved in something that causes them to accrue too much of it which heightens that they may become a victim of the Wyrm. And some Wyrm minions don't detect as the Wyrm at all. There's some room for interaction.<br /> <br /> One of the complements for my games (not just WoD, but other RPGs) that my players give is that they like the scenes where their PCs can talk with the villains. It brings out more of the setting and leads to interesting encounters. So when I run WtA, I want some of that to be possible too. It can be fun for PCs to talk to some important vampire in the city, or an insider in the local PENTEX operation, or some unusual fomori just like how Harry Dresden often talks to lots of villainous antagonists in his books. Some villains aren't even antagonists (at least in some books). Some werewolf PCs are often mindless in their Rage that they would not do that, but the players of those PC usually still want the other werewolf PCs of their pack to still be able to have those scenes. And sometimes I can even arrange for that player whose PC cannot contribute to play someone's Kinfolk, Ally, or some other NPC detailed on some PCs's character sheet in that scene so they can contribute as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T11:14:35-07:00","id":1535287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535274#post1535274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that Vampire players, entrenched into a &quot;degrees of gray&quot; mindset, don't understand that WtA is set in a very black and white setting. Yes, werewolves can have varying degrees of gray morality, but the Wyrm has none of that. Likewise, there's some gray between Technocracy and Traditions, but there is NONE when the subject are the Nefandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more that the vampire players find WtA too simplistic given VtM has no right side. So the thought then goes that the game is limiting itself by not allowing you to play the 'bad guys.' At times the issue can be as simple as finding the save the world-plot too childish.<br /> <br /> It is just ignorance of the setting and trying to fit everything within a single mould.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T11:29:19-07:00","id":1535289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535287#post1535287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is more that the vampire players find WtA too simplistic given VtM has no right side. So the thought then goes that the game is limiting itself by not allowing you to play the 'bad guys.' At times the issue can be as simple as finding the save the world-plot too childish.<br /> <br /> It is just ignorance of the setting and trying to fit everything within a single mould.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hopes? Dreams? Aspirations? That's dumb. You should just be apathetic to everything. Speaking of which, here's my take on Werewolf. I call it a 'Reimagining'.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T14:27:16-07:00","id":1535302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535247#post1535247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Tzims aren't villains, no one is. They call themselves Fiends, turn people into clothing and furniture on a lark, ham up performances as evil bastards, and they love every minute of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the same as saying the Red Talons are all genocidal maniacs.<br /> <br /> My point was that they fulfill similar roles in the game. And on top of that, not all Tzimisce are the same stereotypical asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T20:16:34-07:00","id":1535324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535276#post1535276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just me guessing, but I think you took it more to the side of ABSURD, than EVIL or AMORAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you're familiar with Dark Ages Fae, but the Fairies in that game are pretty alien and have absolutely nothing in common with Changeling the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> He played his character absolutely spot on as designed. For him, the fact that humans were not worshipping the &quot;Fair Folk&quot; and were failing to deliver their end of the bargain on their Oaths and on top of that were &quot;talking gibberish&quot; about some Human-God was more than enough reason to &quot;dispose of them all&quot;.<br /> <br /> That was a perfectly sound logic and reaction for one of the Fae - if you read the game, you'll find that his behavior followed the game expectations to the letter. It took me completely by surprise, but I had to agree that it was an 100% legit reaction given the game's assumptions.<br /> <br /> And he didn't do that act out of evil or malice, he did because in the mind of an alien Far, that's simply what you're supposed to do.<br /> <br /> It's like a relationship between cows and humans. Cows aren't supposed to attack humans, they are supposed to become our food. It's more or less like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T20:25:13-07:00","id":1535327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535284#post1535284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can portray some Wyrm minions with gray morality. After all, vampires are of the Wyrm too, and people are fine representing them in various ways. Obviously on one far side of the spectrum, certain minions of the Wyrm just want to murder the world. But on the other side of the spectrum are just people making deals with the devil to get ahead in life to enjoy power, wealth, desire, etc. They may still do evil acts, but it's much more petty evil or limited in scale. Not every single fomori or monster are so depraved to be utterly unredeemable or have no good side. That doesn't mean they ultimately aren't enemies to the Garou or Gaia, but the Garou can prioritize which Wyrm minions need to be taken down first, or have the usual suspects among the Garou decide it's better to make deals with certain Wyrm minions so they can concentrate on greater threats.<br /> <br /> As ST I do try to have a full spectrum of different types of Wyrm minions (or people beginning to involve themselves with the Wyrm who don't understand what they're doing) so the game isn't completely about combat. Some Wyrm factions are obviously monstrous and need to be wiped out, but others might best be dealt with more subtle means or even negotiation. Some might even be best to ignore because there's so many other things to deal with.<br /> <br /> And since Wyrm taint is so nebulous, not everyone who has Wyrm taint is actually any kind of enemy. They're just been involved in something that causes them to accrue too much of it which heightens that they may become a victim of the Wyrm. And some Wyrm minions don't detect as the Wyrm at all. There's some room for interaction.<br /> <br /> One of the complements for my games (not just WoD, but other RPGs) that my players give is that they like the scenes where their PCs can talk with the villains. It brings out more of the setting and leads to interesting encounters. So when I run WtA, I want some of that to be possible too. It can be fun for PCs to talk to some important vampire in the city, or an insider in the local PENTEX operation, or some unusual fomori just like how Harry Dresden often talks to lots of villainous antagonists in his books. Some villains aren't even antagonists (at least in some books). Some werewolf PCs are often mindless in their Rage that they would not do that, but the players of those PC usually still want the other werewolf PCs of their pack to still be able to have those scenes. And sometimes I can even arrange for that player whose PC cannot contribute to play someone's Kinfolk, Ally, or some other NPC detailed on some PCs's character sheet in that scene so they can contribute as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all that exists sure, but I wasn't referring to that.<br /> <br /> Specifically, BSDs are NOT the type of &quot;innocent victims&quot;. Just like Baalis or Nefandi. Their purpose is to be the big and unequivocal baddies and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T20:28:23-07:00","id":1535328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535289#post1535289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Hopes? Dreams? Aspirations? That's dumb. You should just be apathetic to everything. Speaking of which, here's my take on Werewolf. I call it a 'Reimagining'.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, why play a game upon which you can become a hero filled with hope, when you can be a depressed a hole with 50 shades of jerk built into it in an endless spiral of angst and apathy, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T23:00:03-07:00","id":1535333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533141-making-player-characters-out-of-\u201cvillainous\u201d-factions?p=1535302#post1535302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's the same as saying the Red Talons are all genocidal maniacs.<br /> <br /> My point was that they fulfill similar roles in the game. And on top of that, not all Tzimisce are the same stereotypical asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't know it from reading their splat in V20 or their old Clanbook, though. I'm not really sure that the Revised Clanbook would smooth over those edges, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}